  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Ezekiel",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 23,
    "summary": "Two sisters, Samaria and Jerusalem, committed whoredoms by worshipping idols—Both are destroyed for their lewdness.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The word of the Lord came again unto me, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:1",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Son of man, there were two women, the daughters of one mother:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "Jer. 3:7 (7–8, 10); Ezek. 16:46 (45–46, 61)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:2",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And they committed whoredoms in Egypt; they committed whoredoms in their youth: there were their breasts pressed, and there they bruised the teats of their virginity.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:3",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And the names of them were Aholah the elder, and Aholibah her sister: and they were mine, and they bare sons and daughters. Thus were their names; Samaria is Aholah, and Jerusalem Aholibah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "HEB A tent."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "HEB My tent is in her."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 26
          },
          {
            "start": 129,
            "end": 133
          },
          {
            "start": 155,
            "end": 157
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:4",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And Aholah played the harlot when she was mine; and she doted on her lovers, on the Assyrians her neighbours,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 15:19; 17:6 (3–6); Hosea 8:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 97
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:5",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Which were clothed with blue, captains and rulers, all of them desirable young men, horsemen riding upon horses.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:6",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Thus she committed her whoredoms with them, with all them that were the chosen men of Assyria, and with all on whom she doted: with all their idols she defiled herself.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:7",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Neither left she her whoredoms brought from Egypt: for in her youth they lay with her, and they bruised the breasts of her virginity, and poured their whoredom upon her.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 38
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:8",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore I have delivered her into the hand of her lovers, into the hand of the Assyrians, upon whom she doted.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:9",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "These discovered her nakedness: they took her sons and her daughters, and slew her with the sword: and she became famous among women; for they had executed judgment upon her.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:10",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And when her sister Aholibah saw this, she was more corrupt in her inordinate love than she, and in her whoredoms more than her sister in her whoredoms.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 138,
            "end": 141
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:11",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "She doted upon the Assyrians her neighbours, captains and rulers clothed most gorgeously, horsemen riding upon horses, all of them desirable young men.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 16:7 (7–18); 2 Chr. 28:16 (16–21); Ezek. 16:28."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:12",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Then I saw that she was defiled, that they took both one way,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 37
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:13",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And that she increased her whoredoms: for when she saw men portrayed upon the wall, the images of the Chaldeans portrayed with vermilion,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:14",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Girded with girdles upon their loins, exceeding in dyed attire upon their heads, all of them princes to look to, after the manner of the Babylonians of Chaldea, the land of their nativity:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:15",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And as soon as she saw them with her eyes, she doted upon them, and sent messengers unto them into Chaldea.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ezekiel 23:16",
        "book": "Ezekiel",
        "chapter": 23,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
